    47	
    48	**Motion findings:** motion instants — map highlight sweep ≈0–6000 ms (lead-in, not the technique) · tile fade-in ≈6000–8000 ms · free growth ≈9000–12000 ms · free label/arrows reveal with the growth (≈9500–12000 ms) · free label/arrows removal between 16000 and 18000 ms · enslaved frames + label grow between 20000 and 22000 ms. Holds — small-tile ≈8000–9000 ms · free state with label ≈12000–16000 ms · free state bare ≈18000–20000 ms · enslaved state ≈22000–28000 ms (to ≈298 s at finer sampling). No tile changes camp, ever; the two acts are (1) tile AREA re-set to free population, (2) a FRAME added around South tiles whose thickness carries enslaved population. Tile colour shifts dark grey (small state) → teal (free state) during the growth.
    49	**Camp assignment (census-priced):** 12 tiles. South camp (left + centre columns, under the South header's half): Virginia · North Carolina · South Carolina · Delaware · Maryland · Georgia · New Jersey (7 — New Jersey stands in the centre column grouped with North/South Carolina, on the South half of the stage). North camp (right half): New York · Pennsylvania · Connecticut · Massachusetts · New Hampshire (5). Rhode Island does not appear.
    50	**Size/frame values: VISUAL ESTIMATES** — free sizes and frame thicknesses estimated from the census/ev frames at 640 px against the Pennsylvania anchor (largest free tile); no per-state population table is supplied by the packet, and no measured area-to-population scaling rule is claimed.
    51	**Sub-beats:** SB-A tile fade-in at small size + headers · SB-B growth to free-population area + grey→teal shift · SB-C free label + twin arrows reveal · SB-D free label/arrows removal (bare free hold) · SB-E enslaved frames grow on South tiles + enslaved label/arrow · SB-F final hold.
    52	
    53	### 1.4 Variables (§1.3 extraction)
    54	1. Tile set — per tile: label, camp (south/north), centre position, free width/height (area carries free population), enslaved frame thickness (0 for North tiles).
    55	2. Camp headers — title + subtitle text per camp, header positions, title/sub font sizes.
    56	3. Small state — smallFraction (tile scale in SB-A), tinyFraction (fade-in start scale), tile start fill (dark grey) → free fill (teal) colour shift.
    57	4. Centre labels — free label lines ("Free people population" / "(mostly white)"), enslaved label text, label font sizes, arrow paths (two free arrows, one enslaved arrow), arrow colours/widths.
    58	5. Timing — appear start/duration, free-growth start/duration, free-label start/duration, free-label-out start/duration, enslaved start/duration, final hold, total duration.
    59	6. Palette — paper ground, tile grey, tile teal, enslaved rust, ink, label ink, arrow teal, arrow ink, tile-label white.
    60	7. Tile labels — font family, per-tile font rule (scale with tile width, min/max clamps), line wrapping.
    61	8. Easing — per-phase easing names.
    62	9. Phase order — appear < free growth; free label inside the growth window; label-out after growth; enslaved after label-out (validation-enforced).
    63	
    64	### 1.5 Guidance dispositions (inline, A9.5)
    65	- A1 §2 typography precedent (runtime sampling of config-rendered text): NOT APPLICABLE — no particle typography; all text is DOM/SVG text rendered from CONFIG strings, the same config-driven principle in its DOM form. Reason stated here per A9.5.
    66	- A5 Owner Cures 1–2 (intensity separation · phrase exclusivity): NOT APPLICABLE as particle/sequence cures — no particle field, no phrase lifecycle. The analogous separation here is construction-level: the two counting rules are different KINDS of mark (area vs frame), never the same mark at two intensities; and the two acts are strictly sequential by the phase-order invariant (Owner Cure 2's exclusivity in schedule form).
    67	- A5 §4 flow-field model: NOT APPLICABLE — no particle pool exists in this technique.
    68	- A9.1 plate construction: NOT APPLICABLE — no moving background plate; the ground is the specimen's still paper ground.
    69	- Family: Packet #12 tile/diagram siblings (T210 grid-map PASS 85.2 · T212 margin bars, attempt in completion) — tile geometry from CONFIG arrays is the family's demonstrated construction; T212's filed lesson (receipt-form discipline, A12/A13) is carried into §5 planning.
    70	
    71	## §2 — PLAN
    72	
    73	### 2.1 Parameter table (every variable → CONFIG key; specimen value = default)
    74	Top-level: `stageW 640 · stageH 400 · headerY 18 · campTitleFontPx 30 · campSubFontPx 17 · centreLabelFontPx 21 · centreSubFontPx 14 · enslavedLabelFontPx 20 · tileLabelScale 0.17 · tileLabelMinPx 20 · tileLabelMaxPx 30 · tinyFraction 0.18 · smallFraction 0.5 · arrowWidthPx 3.5 · freeArrowPaths [[[0.80,0.30],[0.72,0.42],[0.66,0.52]], [[0.80,0.30],[0.84,0.44],[0.90,0.54]]] (normalized stage coords, apex→NC, apex→NY) · enslavedArrowPath [[0.66,0.30],[0.60,0.38],[0.55,0.44]] · tAppearMs 0 · appearDurMs 1500 · headerDurMs 800 · tFreeMs 3000 · freeDurMs 3000 · tFreeLabelMs 3500 · freeLabelDurMs 1500 · tFreeLabelOutMs 10000 · freeLabelOutDurMs 1000 · tEnslavedMs 14500 · enslavedDurMs 2000 · holdMs 4500 · easeAppear/easeFree/easeLabel/easeEnslaved all "easeInOut" · palette {ground #f4f1ea, tileStart #4a4a4a, tile #56706b, enslaved #c85a2e, ink #333333, labelInk #2f2f2f, arrowFree #6fa8a0, arrowDark #2f2f2f, tileLabel #ffffff} · fontFamily "Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif" · campSouthTitle "South" · campSouthSub "Pro-slavery" · campNorthTitle "North" · campNorthSub "Anti-slavery" · campSouthX 160 · campNorthX 490 · freeLabelLine1 "Free people population" · freeLabelLine2 "(mostly white)" · freeLabelX 320 · freeLabelY 92 · enslavedLabelText "Enslaved people" · enslavedLabelX 415 · enslavedLabelY 92`.
    75	Derived (named, not stored): tile scale at t (phase interpolation tiny→small→free) · tile fill (tileStart→tile lerp by free progress) · frame thickness = enslavedPx × enslavedP · freeLabelOpacity (in by label phase, out by label-out phase) · completeAtMs = tEnslavedMs + enslavedDurMs · durationMs = completeAtMs + holdMs = 21000. **Phase-order invariant (validation-enforced):** tFreeMs ≥ appear end · free-label end ≤ free growth end + freeLabelDurMs (label reveal rides the growth) · tFreeLabelOutMs ≥ free growth end · tEnslavedMs ≥ label-out end — a violating CONFIG is rejected by validateConfig, never rendered overlapped.
    76	Nested: `tiles[12]` — `{label, camp, cx, cy, freeW, freeH, enslavedPx}` (sizes/thicknesses are the §1.3 VISUAL ESTIMATES at the 640 px stage): Virginia south 105,165 150×135 e15 · North Carolina south 232,150 118×118 e11 · South Carolina south 232,245 84×84 e8 · Delaware south 62,262 44×44 e3 · Maryland south 140,282 96×96 e8 · Georgia south 62,330 58×58 e4 · New Jersey south 232,330 84×84 e3 · New York north 432,168 130×130 e0 · Pennsylvania north 558,152 148×138 e0 · Connecticut north 395,262 94×94 e0 · Massachusetts north 558,262 140×128 e0 · New Hampshire north 452,330 76×84 e0. (Count assertion: tiles source-count 12 = built-count 12, harness-printed.)
    77	Derived (never stored): per-tile scale, fill, frame thickness, label font px = clamp(freeW × tileLabelScale, tileLabelMinPx, tileLabelMaxPx).
    78	
    79	### 2.2 Construction choice
    80	**DOM/SVG tiles + frames (chosen):** one SVG scene; per tile a frame rect (enslaved colour, drawn behind, grown by frame thickness) + a tile rect + centred wrapped text label; two camp header groups; centre label groups with SVG paths for the arrows (dash draw-on for the free arrows, fade for the enslaved arrow) — all geometry from `stateAt(cfg,t)`, a pure function evaluable in node.
    81	Rejected: Canvas 2D — loses per-element ink measurement + DOM label measurement the A6 fit leg needs. CSS keyframes — phase state not evaluable as a pure function (A11 receipts impossible). HTML div tiles — workable, but SVG gives exact rect/frame geometry for harness receipts at less code.
    82	**Named deferrals (lawful, priced):** (1) the colonial-map lead-in (source 271–277 s) — a different visual device (antique map + highlight sweep), not the tile technique; the build opens on the paper ground at the tile lifecycle. (2) State-silhouette glyphs inside tiles — omitted: drawing state outlines from the specimen frames would approach tracing, and the technique's mechanic is area/frame re-categorisation, carried by tile size, frame, and the state NAME label. (3) The three-fifths banner/person at the window tail (source ≈298–305 s) — T219's technique, a separate queue item (#101).
    83	
    84	### 2.3 Census-anchor mapping (A10.2) + A11 assertions
    85	Window-start offset: **t=0 allocation** — build 0 ms = source 277000 ms (segment-relative 6000 ms); build instant = census seg-rel − 6000 for every tile-lifecycle checkpoint. Departure table: census CP0–CP2 (map lead-in, 0–4000 ms) and CP14–CP17 (T219 tail, 28000–34000 ms) have NO build counterpart — named deferrals §2.2 (1) and (3); CP3 (6000 ms, fade) maps to build 0 as the appear phase's zero-state (tiles at tinyFraction, opacity 0).
    86	Assertions (each: CONFIG expression → evaluated instant):
    87	- CP0 zero: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tAppearMs)` → 0 ms: every tile opacity 0, scale = tinyFraction. (Zero-state anchor, guards cmd 8.)
    88	- P1 appear complete: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tAppearMs + CONFIG.appearDurMs)` → 1500 ms: every tile scale = smallFraction, opacity 1; headers opacity 1.
    89	- P2 free mid: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tFreeMs + CONFIG.freeDurMs/2)` → 4500 ms: every tile scale = smallFraction + (1 − smallFraction) × eased(0.5) = 0.75; fill lerp at 0.5.
    90	- P3 free complete: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tFreeMs + CONFIG.freeDurMs)` → 6000 ms: every tile scale 1; freeLabelP = 1 (label end 5000 ≤ 6000).
    91	- P4 label-out mid: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tFreeLabelOutMs + CONFIG.freeLabelOutDurMs/2)` → 10500 ms: freeLabelOpacity = 0.5.
    92	- P5 bare hold: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tFreeLabelOutMs + CONFIG.freeLabelOutDurMs)` → 11000 ms: freeLabelOpacity 0; enslavedP 0; every frame thickness 0.
    93	- P6 enslaved mid: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tEnslavedMs + CONFIG.enslavedDurMs/2)` → 15500 ms: Virginia frame = 15 × eased(0.5) = 7.5; New York frame 0.
    94	- P7 enslaved complete: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tEnslavedMs + CONFIG.enslavedDurMs)` → 16500 ms (= completeAtMs): Virginia frame 15, every South frame = its enslavedPx, every North frame 0.
    95	- P8 hold identity: `stateAt(CONFIG, completeAtMs + 500)` fully equal to P7 state. durationMs = completeAt + holdMs = 21000.
    96	- **Fixed census-instant probes (C*, build instant = census seg-rel − 6000):** C@2000 (census 8000, small-tile state) — scale = smallFraction, freeP 0. C@4000 (census 10000, mid-growth) — 0 < freeP < 1 AND 0 < freeLabelP < 1. C@12000 (census 18000, label gone) — freeLabelOpacity 0, scale 1. C@16000 (census 22000, enslaved present) — enslavedP > 0.5, Virginia frame > 7.5. C@20000 (census 26000, final hold) — state equal to P7.
    97	
    98	### 2.4 Verification plan (instruments named)
    99	- Execute checklist: (1) cut segment.mp4 from source.webm at 270.5–305.5 s (window ±0.5 handles), libx264/yuv420p+AAC faststart, ffprobe filed; (2) build recreation.html (CONFIG at top, pure stateAt, window.__T218 exposed); (3) build comparison.html (shared controls, video.currentTime − 0.5 s handle offset → source ms → build ms = sourceMs − 277000 clamped [0,21000] — during the map lead-in and T219 tail the recreation holds its zero/final state, labeled as the allocation on the comparison face; labels as charged, phone stacking @media ≤560px); (4) own checks §5 legs 1–3.
   100	- Swap test: content — tiles replaced by a 4-tile set {Alpha south 100×100 e10, Beta south 70×70 e5, Gamma north 120×90 e0, Delta north 60×60 e0} at distinct centres (labels/sizes/frames/camps must follow; frame appears only on south tiles); timing — `tEnslavedMs 14500→15500` (P6/P7 probe instants move by the CONFIG expressions: P6 15500→16500, completeAt 16500→17500); phase-order negative test — `tEnslavedMs→9000` must be REJECTED by validateConfig (enslaved before label-out end 11000); palette — `palette.enslaved #c85a2e→#2e7ec8` (observed frame fill in stateAt output + renderer binding).
   101	- Purity: guards cmd1 grep `segment\.mp4|source\.webm|source\.mp4|<video|<img|ajavsMbCapY` → 0 hits; external-reference scan (`src=|href=|@import|url(` → none beyond the SVG namespace identifier); asset inventory = recreation.html alone. Comparison check pass conditions: both labels present verbatim · handle-offset mapping evaluates (video 13.0 s → source 283.5 s → build 6500 ms) · `@media (max-width:560px)` stacking rule present · comparison script `node --check` rc=0.
   102	- A6 legs: fit-table.md (PIL rendered measurement, stand-in font DejaVu Serif named, for camp headers, centre labels, and all 12 tile labels at their CONFIG fonts) + config-census.md (all literals classified; every CONFIG key incl. `tiles[]` nested keys resolved to value-flowing sites; CSS-variable check — none used).
   103	- jev-prewave after legs 1–3 + A6, payload per its contract (A6 outputs verbatim, A10.1); five-lens wave only on FIRE-WAVE; bar avg ≥85, min ≥70.
   104	
   105	### 2.5 Failure points (priced)
   106	- Fitting limits: tile labels at phone width — the fit-floor cure raises small-tile labels above specimen proportion: label font = clamp(freeW × 0.17, 20, 30) px at the 640 stage → minimum ink height ≈11.2 px at 360; Delaware's label (44 px tile, 20 px font) overflows its tile symmetrically, centred, rendered over the tile with a halo — a named departure from the specimen, priced here, measured in the fit leg (the T212 font-raise precedent).
   107	- Allocation-vs-census timing: the t=0 allocation discards the map lead-in's 6 s and T219's 7 s tail; if a timing lens prices the build against the full 34 s window instead of the tile lifecycle, the departure table (§2.3) is the priced answer, filed before the wave.
   108	- Frame-vs-area confusion: the enslaved act must read as ADDED population (frame outside the free tile), never as a resize — frames draw behind the tile rect and grow outward only; tile scale stays 1 through SB-E/F (asserted in P6/P7: scale unchanged vs P5).
   109	- Camp-assignment dispute: New Jersey's centre-column placement is priced as South by stage half (§1.3); a lens reading it as North is answered by the census column position, filed here in advance.
   110	- Silhouette absence: tiles carry no state outlines (named deferral §2.2 (2)); the readability/motion lenses may price the plainer tile — accepted risk, the name label carries identity.
   111	- Render-proof limitation: no browser binary in this seat — PIXEL-UNVERIFIED carried to scores.md; comparison page is the render surface.
   112	- Plateau (A2): FIRST ATTEMPT — no prior average; a FAIL files its WHY in scores.md and routes attempt 2 to practice. **Predicted minimum lens: motion fidelity** — hypothesis: the specimen's growth is a continuous area morph of irregular tiles while the build interpolates uniform scale about each tile centre, and the omitted silhouettes/map lead-in are motion-visible departures; if the wave's minimum is not motion, the WHY section names the actual stuck lens and its cause instead.
